# Duet firmware files that a separately published build replaces.
#
# One line per file:
#
#   <file> sha256:<checksum of the published build> <https location>
#
# The file has to be one the reprapfirmware package delivers below
# /opt/dsf/sd/firmware, because that is the name RepRapFirmware derives from
# the board type when it flashes; a build under any other name is never used.
# Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local path, no
# fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Replacing a Duet firmware file"
# in the README, in particular why the build needs a version string of its
# own before any board is flashed with it.
#
# Example:
#   Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:0123...cdef https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/v3.7.0-rc.1+mp1/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:337d742566314111ae9fc910c5c6586ad784de85a282460a094494e4bd70914f https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.8/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin sha256:4c87ecdf39b084dc35de5c80fd3ec62c8433b6a77579159c16270cad0992db46 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.8/Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin
Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin sha256:76f61f4714b1eeefd1240d7b5b37f578f62c53de28f68518b8e2899d259a180c https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.8/Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin
# Mainboard: RepRapFirmware 3.7-dev at upstream 3.7.0-rc.1+3 (5862b26), built
# by us against the Meltingplot library forks with a version string of its
# own, so DuetControlServer flashes it on an image update. From 5862b26 on,
# the firmware reports its accelerometers under sensors.accelerometers, where
# DuetSoftwareFramework 3.7.0-rc.2 looks for them; 3.7.0-rc.1 does not.
Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin sha256:15c4774f0a31ce2eaf4839429dbb047fe2f485abdb3bc903a1ea71e19cf481f1 https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.6/Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin
